%% fsm-contract: {"eventType":"exercise","askedFields":["occurredAt","intensity","duration","activityType"],"path":["occurredAt","intensity","duration","activityType","optional-context","stored"],"globalStateChange":false,"lifecycleChange":false,"emergencyImpact":true,"priorityImpact":false,"medicalReasoning":false}
%% Same shape as meal.mmd's fsm-contract; not yet enforced by test/fsm_mermaid_contract_test.dart.
flowchart TD
  INPUT[Exercise event from user or parser] --> TIME[Ask if it happened now or at another time]
  TIME --> INTENSITY[Ask intensity: leve, moderada, or intensa]
  INTENSITY --> DURATION[Ask duration in minutes]
  DURATION --> ACTIVITY[Ask activity type, free text]
  ACTIVITY --> CONTEXT[Offer optional context]
  CONTEXT --> STORE[Store exercise event]
  STORE --> SIGNAL[Feeds recentIntenseExercise signal to EmergencyEngine]

  NOTE[Generic missing-field collection only: no new DiabAIGlobalState, EventStatus, priority rule, or medical recommendation. duration is a plain FieldSpec like intensity, so it can also be pre-filled passively from the parser's duration entity before being asked.]
  TIME_NOTE[occurredAt is the shared eventTimeField (see events.dart) prepended generically by KnowledgeEngine.missingFields to every event type's own fields — not exercise-specific. Answering it also confirms/overwrites EventInstance.createdAt with the real clock time before storage. Distinct from the duration field itself, which is the exercise's own length, not its start time.]
  BACKLOG[Roadmap backlog, not implemented: energy-expenditure estimate, dedicated history view. Predicted glycemic impact is medical reasoning and stays out of scope per AGENTS.md.]
